1325995807818486852,Horserider's home - with view of pyramids+terrace,https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1325995807818486852?locale=en-US&currency=USD&check_in=2026-05-19&check_out=2026-05-24,https://a0.muscache.com/im/pictures/hosting/Hosting-U3RheVN1cHBseUxpc3Rpbmc6MTMyNTk5NTgwNzgxODQ4Njg1Mg==/original/582dadd0-d705-41c5-bad3-eeab39b71633.jpeg,29.9679,31.1437,4.94,112.0,4.98,5.0,4.97,4.82,182,$237,0,"We rear and unique in Giza! Bedroom is a part of our home/horse farm with a queen bed (160x200cm)  and its own shower. Corner  BEST room with open views to desert and pyramids. Opens to large shared terrace. The room is a corner room and just above the street, so you hear local street noise - horses, visitors sitting downstairs  etc.. Remember - egypt never sleeps ! No wifi available, please obtain local sim with data on arrival.Fans free  , AC and heating at 3Euro per nightNO ORFIThe space⏰ CHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICYNO EARLY CHECK-IN / NO LATE CHECK-OUT• Check-in: after 2:00 PM• Check-out: by 11:00 AMIf you wish to arrive earlier or leave later, please book an extra night to avoid disappointment.🎒 BAG STORAGE / DROP-OFF ONLYAvailable while the house is being prepared.This is drop-off only — no hanging out around the house.• Small bag: 100 EGP (≈ $3 USD)• Large bag: 200 EGP (≈ $6 USD)🌿 ABOUT THE PLACE – PLEASE READ CAREFULLYThis is a simple, farm-style home, oriented toward eco-sustainable living.The room is located above our stables, home to 80+ horses and donkeys 🐎. • Accessed by stairs through the stables entrance• This is a self-catering HOME, not a hotel — expect a homely atmosphere.•  there is NO room service nor servants. You carry your bags, bring your own cigarettes and take care of room cleanliness etc. If you like bedding and towels changed daily there will be an additional charge. We have NO room service nor servants. You carry your bags, make your own tea, bring your own capsules for coffee machine and take care of room cleanliness etc. If you like bedding and towels changed daily, additional toilet paper there will be additional charge. This listing is not just about the room itself, but also about the location. Unfortunately, many guests do not read the full description, especially the notes about the surroundings, and then we are penalized in ratings for things that are clearly disclosed and beyond our control.Egypt has a very specific lifestyle and environment, and where we are is a very old shabby area. We are located above multiple stables and surrounded by mosques, people riding horses 24/7, locals have goats and roosters on roof tops, which means there can be animal sounds and call to prayer. This is stated in the listing, but these elements cannot be changed or silenced. Thats why the cost of the room is lower than other kind of same quality accommodation which should be appreciated not low rated. That's why I sent you a message to give attention to these details.⚡ ELECTRICITY & SUSTAINABILITYEgypt experiences occasional electricity shortages, which are beyond our control.Please be mindful:• Lights OFF when not in use• Do not leave lights on when leaving the room or apartmentIf lights are left on, we will switch them off (by entering the room if needed).Please help us protect the environment 🌍 and reduce waste.🛏️ AMENITIES• Bedding & towels provided• No hairdryer available• NO Wi-Fi — please arrange an eSIM or local SIM for internet• Fan provided free of charge• Heating & A/C available at €3 per day per unit• Universal power sockets (one includes USB)👧 CHILD POLICYChildren over 10 years old are welcome under full parental supervision.Please note:• Animals, cactus, stairs, terraces, and multiple levels• No kids’ entertainment providedParents are fully responsible for their child’s safety and free time.🇪🇬 IMPORTANT – EGYPTIAN GUESTSNO ORFIOnly officially registered marriages are accepted, in accordance with local law.NO VISITORS from outside allowed. No drivers, friends or your tour guides , this is our home not a public place.Guest accessHouse open areas are shared with us and other guests. You may use all terraces in respectful way.📍 LOCATION & ARRIVALOur street is unique — full of horses, donkeys, and camels. Not easy to find, but that’s old Giza charm! You’ll enjoy open Pyramid views and spacious outdoor areas.If you want tourist hustle right at the Pyramid gate, this is not the place for you. Museums & Pyramids are 9–20 min by foot or car, markets & restaurants just 5 min away by tuk-tuk or walk.Recommended: Use our trusted drivers.• English-speaking & know the area• Will show you the house, doors, and room• Arrival is stress-freeIf you take your own transport, follow our Google Maps location carefully. Most drivers don’t know our street, and we cannot provide assistance at night.⚠️ Arrival on your own is at your own risk — no refunds if the driver gets lost.INTERACTION WITH GUESTSHOST INTERACTIONWe live on the property, so we are often around and available if needed.However, please understand that we run a busy household and equestrian place, so we cannot spend long hours socializing or giving history lessons. We kindly ask guests to do their own research before arrival.When time allows, we are happy to interact, assist, and help with practical matters.OTHER DETAILSPLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE BOOKINGWe live in Masr (not “Egypt” as a concept 😉 — Google the difference!)This is a desert & horse-stables area, not a city or resort location.⚠️ If you don’t like animals, this is NOT the place for you. Sorry.🐎 ANIMALS & ENVIRONMENTWe live above active horse stables, so please expect:• Natural smells at times• Sounds from horses and donkeys (horses love talking 😄)• Flies, dust• Local noise especially on weekends as many riders come to the area to enjoy late nights and early ridesWe also share our home with:• 🐱 Shaqia, our very curious and friendly cat (she loves sleeping on beds)• 🐶 Two rescued chihuahuas — friendly but still cautious with new people(They love guests and treats — limited please, ask first!)This is a very Egyptian, authentic environment.❌ Do NOT expect 5-star streets or polished surroundings.✔ Expect simple, real local life, very different from downtown or tourist areas.We have dust, flies, desert air, and nature — this is part of where we live and what we love.If you are not open-minded or sensitive to these realities, this place may not suit you.🏜️ LOCATION & SURROUNDINGS• Desert & stables area• We do not control street activity• Supermarket just a few minutes’ walk for basics• We can take you to a local market for vegetables, fruits, and moreDuring your stayWe live on the property, so we are often around and available if needed.However, please understand that we run a busy household and equestrian place, so we cannot spend long hours socializing or giving history lessons. We kindly ask guests to do their own research before arrival.When time allows, we are happy to interact, assist, and help with practical matters.Other things to notePLEASE READ CAREFULLY BEFORE BOOKINGWe live in Masr (not “Egypt” as a concept 😉 — Google the difference!)This is a desert & horse-stables area, not a city or resort location.⚠️ If you don’t like animals, this is NOT the place for you. Sorry.🐎 ANIMALS & ENVIRONMENTWe live above active horse stables, so please expect:• Natural smells at times• Sounds from horses and donkeys (horses love talking 😄)• Flies, dust• Local noise especially on weekends as many riders come to the area to enjoy late nights and early ridesWe also share our home with:• 🐱 Shaqia, our very curious and friendly cat (she loves sleeping on beds)• 🐶 Two rescued chihuahuas — friendly but still cautious with new people(They love guests and treats — limited please, ask first!)This is a very Egyptian, authentic environment.❌ Do NOT expect 5-star streets or polished surroundings.✔ Expect simple, real local life, very different from downtown or tourist areas.We have dust, flies, desert air, and nature — this is part of where we live and what we love.If you are not open-minded or sensitive to these realities, this place may not suit you.🏜️ LOCATION & SURROUNDINGS• Desert & stables area• We do not control street activity• Supermarket just a few minutes’ walk for basics• We can take you to a local market for vegetables, fruits, and more🌱 SUSTAINABILITY• Drinking water filters provided• We recycle almost everything🧺 LAUNDRY SERVICELaundry available at additional cost:• €3 per load• Large-capacity, top-load machines only• No small loads. Guest hangs items themselves after washing.If you need specific washing requirements, we recommend using a city laundry service (we can’t recommend one as we don’t use them ourselves).🍳 BREAKFASTLocal-style breakfast available at €3 per person (on request).EXPERIENCES & EXTRAS (ON REQUEST)As we operate a professional equestrian facility, we offer the following activities:• Horse riding lessons• Horse carriage rides to the Pyramids• Sunrise / sunset desert rides• Horse riding to the Pyramids or desert💶 From €25 per person per hourWELLNESS & FOOD• Full-body massage, foot massage, and other treatments available• BBQ or Egyptian home-cooked meals available by request only– Pre-booking and pre-payment required– Price depends on number of guests and selected menu– Not available on short noticeDRINKS & SHISHA• Shisha, local coffee, and tea available from the downstairs coffee shop• Can also be provided by us at an additional charge🏠 HOUSE RULES – VERY IMPORTANT• NO outside guests allowed(No drivers, friends, guides, or visitors — this is our home not a public place)• NO ORFI (unless 2 rooms booked)• Please treat the home with care —many mismatched or damaged items are sadly from previous stays.This is a unique place, run with love, animals, dust, imperfections, and heart.We promise to do our best for you, as long as expectations are realistic 🤍",True,1549,True,False,True,,pyramids
