1140397074391194529,Amigos Amarena. Lovely healing Experience,https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1140397074391194529?locale=en-US&currency=USD&check_in=2026-05-20&check_out=2026-05-25,https://a0.muscache.com/im/pictures/hosting/Hosting-1140397074391194529/original/02f4e853-b350-467d-b35c-8e5738426403.jpeg,29.9686,31.1061,4.88,125.0,4.88,4.87,4.76,4.58,762,$895,0,"Private and exclusive unique one bedroom apartment facing the Grand Pyramids.The spaceAmigos Amarena is a 50 Sqm.  of pure luxury one bedroom apartment with a fabulous design, Breath taking view of the Grand Pyramids. Hand crafted wood furniture and the latest appliances that will make you feel at home.a 10 Sqm. balcony that will make you feel you have visited the Pyramids without leaving you place.A large Jacuzzi with bubbles that will tickle you while sipping wine.Built-in King size bed and an additional 180 cm sofa bed if you need to have an extra guest. State of the art bathroom and a full kitchen if you fancy home cooking.We are situated in Hadayek Al-Ahram (Pyramids Garden) a buzzing and peaceful area with security gates filled with restaurants, coffee shops, supermarkets and pharmacies.We will to provide you with a memorable lifetime experience filled with excitement, Tranquility and Comfort.Join us and leave the rest to us.Experience ultimate relaxation and intimacy at our accommodation, where every detail is designed to enhance your stay.✔️ Amarena’s  design offers: ~ Queen size bed by 180 cmx200 cm and concrete nature wood wardrobe~ Clean sheets and blanket~ Smart TV~ A/C- Wi-Fi high speed- outdoor table and 2 outdoor chair✔️ Fully equipped kitchenette~ Microwave~ Cooktop~ Mini fridge~ All the essential kitchen utensils provided✔️ Amenities~ JacuzziGuest accessThe entire apartment is private and exclusive to the situated guests only.Other things to noteCopies of Passports of IDs are required for all guests. As only registered guest is allowed",True,247,True,True,False,"""The main view""",nan
548357234359742514,Soulful Garden Studio in Lush Cairo Neighborhood,https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/548357234359742514?locale=en-US&currency=USD&check_in=2026-05-24&check_out=2026-05-29,https://a0.muscache.com/im/pictures/hosting/Hosting-548357234359742514/original/4d7565d5-a9b3-4c1c-bfd0-eb6d4c47bc00.jpeg,29.95906,31.26202,4.98,195.0,4.97,4.97,4.87,4.93,639,639,0,"Unwind in this fairytale tiny house in a lush Maadi garden, a walkable Cairo neighborhood known for its safety, greenery, and great places to eat. Sustainably built and styled with antique and vintage furniture and decor, this romantic studio includes a bedroom with a kitchenette and a bathroom, as well as an office space accessible from the garden. The magical shared garden features lounging & dining areas, a hammock, an outdoor kitchen with a pizza oven, and a fountain to set the mood.The spaceThe little jewelry box of a studio sleeps 2 people, and includes a comfortable double bed, a tv hidden away behind a repurposed handcarved screen, and an elegant antique Syrian mother-of-pearl dresser. A small, but well-equipped kitchenette with an under-counter mini fridge, microwave, portable stovetop, appliances, and cooking/dining accessories serve your basic cooking needs, and a comfortable bathroom with an antique marble sink and double walk-in shower is a bliss after a long day exploring the busy capital. A cozy and bright private office space with a desk and comfortable love seat for reading breaks can be accessed from the garden. The patio boasts an outdoor kitchen with a wood-fired pizza oven (which with some preparation, cooks perfect pizzas in less than 90 seconds), a barbeque, and potted herbs for your seasoning needs, as well as covered seating for cozy open-air breakfast or dinners. A lounging area, perfect for coffee/tea and conversations can be found at the other end of the garden's lawn, as is a hammock. Adding to the ambience is a beautiful fountain made from reclaimed materials, that doubles as a shallow dipping pool for those hot summer days.Behind beautifully carved reclaimed doors, in a separate tiny building down the limestone path, you’ll find a laundry room and an extra restroom.Guest accessThe Garden StudioOther things to noteWe value the biodiversity and local ecosystem of our urban garden that consist of bats, songbirds, lizards, praying mantises, dragonflies, and more, and we will never use chemical spray or pesticides outside or inside.Therefore, despite our best efforts, a stray bug, spider, or other garden creature may occasionally wander inside, especially if the door to the room is left open.Reservations of this property through Airbnb are for regular stays only, and excludes commercial or event usage. Please read the house rules for more information.Please note that this property is listed under the TINY HOME specialty category on Airbnb. This is NOT a full-size apartment, but rather a studio with an adjacent workspace room, all in a mini cottage of approximately 20 square meters, lovingly built with antique and reclaimed panels and materials.",True,433,False,True,False,Maadi garden,nan
