846283079041523899,Lotus room ‘House of Kheops’,https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/846283079041523899?locale=en-US&currency=USD&check_in=2026-05-01&check_out=2026-05-06,https://a0.muscache.com/im/pictures/miso/Hosting-846283079041523899/original/0c01ed97-53a8-471e-80f5-3a992eef118e.jpeg,29.9809,31.1401,4.79,14.0,4.86,4.79,4.57,4.5,"1,184","1,184",0,"This beautiful room is located directly in front of our observatory, providing stunning views of the night sky and the Great Pyramid! The Lotus Room is designed with tasteful decor that helps artists and individuals to relax and recharge.You can listen to the birds chirping outside your window and take in the peaceful surroundings. This is the perfect place to unwind after a long day of exploring the local area or working on your creative projects.The spaceHouse of Kheops is a spiritual oasis located on the Giza Necropolis plateau, built in alignment with the pyramid of Khufu. The house welcomes all people and aims to share the magical experience of the location and the history of the culture. Guests can wake up and fall asleep with the pyramids visible from the home, gaining a deeper appreciation for their immense scale and history. The house aims to provide a profound sense of peace, wonder, and connection to history for its guests.In addition to its location and atmosphere, House of Kheops also values its principles, which include creating a sense of family and community for its guests. The house was once filled with nature and beings, and it still is to this day. Guests are encouraged to come with an open mind and with no expectation of perfection as it does not exist.The house consists of 4 double bedrooms and a beautiful upstairs sitting room where the pyramid may be viewed through the design and eyes of Stephane Malka. The furniture gifted by renowned artist Christian Hook for his wonderful experience whilst at the house and which inspired his latest artwork collection Sahara. The house has its own water well which we built to provide fresh water to our home and rest of the community. It may be booked as a private villa or when not booked for single use as separate guest rooms in the house.• Whole Villa: https://www.airbnb.com/h/houseofkheops• Olive Room: https://www.airbnb.com/h/oliveroom-hok• Jasmine Room: https://www.airbnb.com/h/jasmineroom-hok• Hibiscus Room: https://www.airbnb.com/h/hibiscusroom-hokAll our welcome, Egyptians must be married by law to stay at the house.We hope you have a wonderful stay!Guest accessOther than your room and private bathroom. You get to access the kitchen/utility room, pool, garden and observatory.During your stayThe House is a shared guest house so interaction between other guests is  encouraged. However, we also fully respect those that look for peace and quiet and so this is also welcomed.Salem, the house manager, will be in the house most of the time, to offer assistance, advise, food options and toursOther things to noteCats may jump on the table while you're eating, so we typically keep a water sprayer nearby to discourage them :)) If you encounter a cute white cate, that’s Clause, give him love and affection, and he will surely reciprocate!",True,459,False,True,False,The main view or location feature,nan
